            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0433" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/568: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-22T11:00:00-00:44">May 22, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>159. Referring to my 158, May 21. On reconsideration Secretary Simpson, by
                    President’s instructions, notified Wehrle last evening of invitation for all
                    Germans to leave Liberia. It is understood five will leave tomorrow by plane and
                    all others are given 2 weeks within which to depart. Any further developments
                    will be telegraphed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
